{
	"_comment": "GLYPHFALL - a world made of text characters (issue #159). Somebody described a valley so carefully that the description became the place: the grass is quote marks, the water is tildes, the trees are clubs and spades, and the paths are the writer's sentences, readable as you walk. A walk-and-wonder world (no goal, no puzzle). Seven regions: the Margin (where you arrive), the Footnotes, the Inkwell, First Lines (the Long Sentence runs across it), Paragraph Wood (trees set in paragraphs), the Heading and the Unwritten. It is an ordinary meadow world underneath; 'atmosphere.glyphs' lays one layer over it (GlyphPage) that writes the finished picture again as monospace characters, and its 'art' block tunes the shared meadow art so each material's colour picks the right characters. Its secret is one wrong glyph: see the 'secret' block (reveal type 'misprint'). Generated by tools/gen_glyphfall_world.py (atlas: pokepals/tools/gen_glyphfall.py) - edit that and re-run, don't hand-tune positions.",
